<title>UK: ALPINE SKIING-KJUS WINS MEN'S DOWNHILL.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-KJUS WINS MEN'S DOWNHILL.</headline>
<dateline>KVITFJELL, Norway 1997-03-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norway's Lasse Kjus won an Alpine skiing World Cup men's downhill on Sunday in one minute 27.12 seconds, according to unofficial results.</p>
<p>Pietro Vitalini of Italy was second in 1:27.26 and Canada's Edi Podivinsky third in 1:27.26, according to unofficial results.</p>
